1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:02,267
Water can get hotter
than boiling —

2
00:00:02,267 --> 00:00:03,567
and still not boil.

3
00:00:03,867 --> 00:00:06,067
Boiling needs
somewhere to start.

4
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:07,133
Bubbles usually form

5
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:09,467
around tiny impurities
in the water.

6
00:00:09,733 --> 00:00:12,400
Heat plain water by itself
in a very clean cup,

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,133
and it can climb past boiling

8
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:16,267
while looking completely calm.

9
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,967
Then a small disturbance —

10
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:19,267
picking up the cup,

11
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:20,967
adding a spoonful of coffee —

12
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:23,267
and bubbles burst
out all at once.

13
00:00:23,267 --> 00:00:25,433
Boiling water can erupt
from the cup.

14
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,033
So don't heat water longer

15
00:00:27,033 --> 00:00:29,167
than the instructions
recommend.

16
00:00:29,167 --> 00:00:31,400
And adding instant
coffee or sugar

17
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,333
before heating greatly
reduces the risk.

18
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:37,400
Calm doesn't always
mean below boiling.

19
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,267
That water may just be waiting
for a reason to boil.
